{#
  The one post card.

  It used to exist four ways: hardcoded six times in index.njk, again in
  culture.njk, again in whats-new.njk, and a fourth time as a template string in
  search.js's resultCard. The homepage copies carried hand-written excerpts and
  hand-picked images, which is how two of them ended up pointing at posts that
  do not exist (the import dropped the records but kept their images).

  `withExcerpt` adds the lead-in sentence and the fade-in on the figure. Both
  the homepage and the archives pass true; it is off only where a caller wants
  the bare card. The excerpt is derived from the post body rather than written
  out, so it cannot drift from the record.
#}
{#- `level` is the card title's heading level. It is a parameter because the two
    callers sit at different depths: on an archive the cards are the page's own
    top-level content, directly under the <h1>, so they are h2; on the homepage
    they sit under a "Culture" / "What's New" section <h2>, so they are h3.
    Hardcoding h3 made every archive page's outline skip a level. -#}
{% macro postCard(post, withExcerpt = false, level = 3) %}
<article class="card">
	<a class="card__link" href="{{ post.data.category | categoryPath }}{{ post.data.slug }}/">
		{%- if post.data.images.length %}
		<figure class="card__figure{% if withExcerpt %} reveal reveal--fade{% endif %}">
			{#- alt="" to match team-card.njk: the <h3> six lines down is inside this
		    same <a>, so repeating the title here had every card announce its name
		    twice. The `| safe` that was on it also emitted unescaped content into
		    an attribute — a title containing a quote would have broken out of it. -#}
		<img src="{{ post.data.images[0] }}" alt="" loading="lazy">
		</figure>
		{%- endif %}
		<div class="card__body">
			{%- if post.data.published %}
			<time class="card__date" datetime="{{ post.data.published | isoDate }}">{{ post.data.published | longDate }}</time>
			{%- endif %}
			<h{{ level }} class="card__title">{{ post.data.title }}</h{{ level }}>
			<p class="card__excerpt">{% if withExcerpt %}{{ post.content | plainText | truncate(150) }} {% endif %}<span class="card__more">Read More</span></p>
		</div>
	</a>
</article>
{% endmacro %}
